Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:40:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] M2-C2b4 b4-3 root cause: mm NaN is ggml-vulkan MUL_MAT_ID
 vs route-B w3d shell, NOT arena/data/graph. Evidence (env-gated tools kept):
 (1) L0 incremental-fill dump (STREAM_MOE_L0INC) - c00 NaN@2348 from prefix1
 alone, byte-stable across all 14 prefixes (rules out graph-order/clobber);
 (2) per-layer CURDUMP - L0 cur is NaN-free (earlier all-QNaN was L29 file
 overwrite artifact; L1+ NaN = L0 mm NaN propagation); (3) LOADDBG at
 mark_ready - vram slot bytes == RAM slot bytes for same (L0,E79) (load/DIO
 correct); (4) VMMDUMP of v1 exec_mm_vk single-node vulkan mm readback =
 byte-identical to arena's wrong output (both NaN 457437, all words differ
 from CPU) - proves v1 'all-vram vulkan mm correct' was a CPU-path artifact,
 vulkan mul_mat_id never computed this shell correctly. CPU runs same w3d
 shell + same data -> correct (cpu_ref IDENTICAL). Next: fix vulkan mul_mat_id
 indexing for ne[2]=n_slots/nb[2]=expert_size virtual 3D weight, or re-layout
 weights to vulkan-native expert-major before upload. RAM IDENTICAL.

